WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.540
judge moved to another stall in the market.

2
00:00:19.941 --> 00:00:21.501
Mazatl stared dreamily.

3
00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:25.662
“I wish I could be a judge someday,” he sighed.

4
00:00:25.682 --> 00:00:28.843
“Maybe you can,” Vinnie said.

5
00:00:29.844 --> 00:00:31.104
Mazatl shook his head.

6
00:00:32.044 --> 00:00:34.725
“Papa is a farmer, so I will be one too.

7
00:00:35.586 --> 00:00:37.026
Judges come from rich homes.

8
00:00:37.526 --> 00:00:38.147
I do not.”

9
00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:42.148
“That’s not fair,” said Vinnie.

10
00:00:42.828 --> 00:00:43.789
Mazatl shrugged.

11
00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:46.570
“Only the gods can direct your life.

12
00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.391
I was meant to be a farmer, I guess.”

13
00:00:50.452 --> 00:00:52.412
Vinnie felt sorry for Mazatl.

14
00:00:53.513 --> 00:00:56.934
Mandy noticed that the Aztec people didn’t use money.

15
00:00:58.055 --> 00:01:01.016
They traded things they had for the things they needed.

16
00:01:02.268 --> 00:01:04.709
She remembered the man selling cocoa beans.

17
00:01:04.729 --> 00:01:07.631
“Are cocoa beans worth much?”

18
00:01:08.071 --> 00:01:08.832
Mandy asked.

19
00:01:10.893 --> 00:01:11.833
Mazatl nodded.

20
00:01:11.853 --> 00:01:14.915
“We use cocoa beans to make a chocolate drink.

21
00:01:15.495 --> 00:01:16.336
It’s our favorite.

22
00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.297
But it is too costly for my family.”

23
00:01:19.998 --> 00:01:21.719
That gave Mandy an idea.

24
00:01:22.899 --> 00:01:27.622
As Mazatl and Vinnie walked along, Mandy went to the cocoa bean seller.

25
00:01:27.642 --> 00:01:32.636
“Sir, I would like to buy your beans,” she said.

26
00:01:33.716 --> 00:01:35.177
He looked at her and laughed.

27
00:01:36.137 --> 00:01:37.898
“What will you give me, little girl?”

28
00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:39.038
he asked.

29
00:01:40.098 --> 00:01:43.779
“Something very precious,” she said bravely.

30
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.140
The bean seller looked at her coldly.

31
00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.341
“Show me.”

32
00:01:50.781 --> 00:01:52.422
Mandy held out her arm.

33
00:01:53.382 --> 00:01:55.122
Her bead bracelet sparkled.

34
00:01:56.023 --> 00:01:57.763
The man’s eyes grew greedy.

35
00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.404
“Where did you get that?”

36
00:01:59.904 --> 00:02:00.604
he demanded.

37
00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:04.470
“From a faraway land,” she replied.

38
00:02:05.631 --> 00:02:08.453
The man stared and then handed over the beans.

39
00:02:09.674 --> 00:02:11.355
Mandy gave him the bracelet.

40
00:02:11.375 --> 00:02:16.059
“Good day, sir,” she said, and ran to find her brother.

41
00:02:17.199 --> 00:02:20.262
Vinnie and Mazatl were going to meet Mazatl’s papa.

42
00:02:21.322 --> 00:02:24.545
Suddenly, Vinnie heard people cheering and shouting.

43
00:02:25.686 --> 00:02:28.788
Attracted by the sounds, he left Mazatl’s side.

44
00:02:31.004 --> 00:02:35.887
Not far away, Vinnie was amazed to find a large outdoor stadium.

45
00:02:36.647 --> 00:02:39.829
Two teams were playing a game similar to basketball.

46
00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:45.152
The players were trying to get a hard rubber ball into a high hoop.

47
00:02:47.253 --> 00:02:52.416
They did not use their hands or feet, only their elbows, hips, and knees.

48
00:02:52.436 --> 00:02:54.778
“That’s impossible!”

49
00:02:55.518 --> 00:02:56.178
Vinnie said.

50
00:02:57.239 --> 00:02:58.960
Then something else caught his eye.

51
00:02:59.888 --> 00:03:02.410
Behind the stadium was a tall tower.

52
00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:08.214
It looked like a pyramid, but the top was flat and had two buildings on it.

53
00:03:09.375 --> 00:03:12.137
Many steps led up to the top of the pyramid.

54
00:03:12.957 --> 00:03:14.718
“I wonder what that is?”

55
00:03:15.419 --> 00:03:15.939
he said.

56
00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:22.343
Meanwhile, Mandy found Mazatl near his father’s stall.

57
00:03:23.244 --> 00:03:25.546
She handed him the bag of cocoa beans.

58
00:03:25.566 --> 00:03:28.588
“But how?”

59
00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.881
Mazatl asked, amazed.

60
00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:34.864
“Please, it is my gift to your family.

61
00:03:36.005 --> 00:03:39.307
You have been so kind to us,” she said.

62
00:03:39.327 --> 00:03:40.908
“Who are you?”

63
00:03:41.408 --> 00:03:42.469
he asked suddenly.

64
00:03:42.489 --> 00:03:44.550
“You are different from us.”

65
00:03:46.712 --> 00:03:50.334
But before she could reply, loud drums began beating.

66
00:03:50.354 --> 00:03:53.156
“Mazatl!” said his father.

67
00:03:53.176 --> 00:03:55.918
“The sacrifices are about to begin.

68
00:03:56.579 --> 00:03:58.500
Let us go to the temple immediately.”

69
00:03:59.249 --> 00:04:00.414
Mandy looked around.

70
00:04:00.434 --> 00:04:02.122
“Where’s Vinnie?”

71
00:04:02.624 --> 00:04:03.166
she asked.
